{"classification":"mathematical-false-converse-hypothesis","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0064","math_ordinal":100,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The converse identifies the arbitrary-index sum with the series over J; this is false if nonzero terms lie outside J. Taking J to be the complete nonzero support is exactly the condition constructed in the preceding paragraph and makes the converse valid.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt226.tex:192","source_normalized_sha256":"3920e623131fea3b6aff245f7083aaba25f22dcde88733a30b2f44b254b43005","source_text":"$J\\subseteq\\{i:a_i\\ne 0\\}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt226.tex:192","target_normalized_sha256":"5bb090a2063cf82e49acef5e571be5d763fbca2301dc0867ebccd6a0055c8634","target_text":"$J=\\{i:a_i\\ne 0\\}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S226"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unbound-projection-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0065","math_ordinal":113,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"K is intended to be the first-coordinate projection of the finite set M, but j is free in the authority set-builder. The existential quantifier closes the definition and gives the finite projection used below.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt226.tex:210","source_normalized_sha256":"b98fca015cf9476f81fc95d9a7803b222e02f753e47cc1481e61a97ccb032d4d","source_text":"$K=\\{i:(i,j)\\in M\\}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt226.tex:210","target_normalized_sha256":"05b9ea1ed03c619967935f79f8a7a5d68b48714dac72ad5dd7a8d1297d8c44e9","target_text":"$K=\\{i:\\exists j\\ (i,j)\\in M\\}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S226"}
{"classification":"mathematical-unbound-projection-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0066","math_ordinal":114,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"L is intended to be the second-coordinate projection of the finite set M, but i is free in the authority set-builder. The existential quantifier closes the definition and gives the finite projection used below.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt226.tex:211","source_normalized_sha256":"dec015c74514408ec8675b5c0b7ccafac633f8447132a32393f318b623068973","source_text":"$L=\\{j:(i,j)\\in M\\}$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt226.tex:211","target_normalized_sha256":"a3035ffdc8e231a132ba6a82bed8908abc3ff2008b0642ff439952b492b264ef","target_text":"$L=\\{j:\\exists i\\ (i,j)\\in M\\}$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S226"}
{"classification":"cross-reference-wrong-subsection","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0067","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Subsection 226B(a) defines saltus functions and their associated families; 226B(b) only defines one-sided-limit notation. The reference must therefore point to (a).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt226.tex:281","source_text":"as defined in (b)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt226.tex:282","target_text":"sebagaimana didefinisikan dalam (a)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S226"}
{"classification":"source-editorial-missing-conjunction","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0068","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH22-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The intended four-family list is determined by the immediately preceding definitions; supplying the missing final conjunction repairs the syntax without changing any formula or assertion.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt226.tex:403-407","source_text":"four-family list lacks a conjunction between the u-double-prime and v-double-prime families","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt226.tex:411-415","target_text":"empat keluarga dipisahkan dengan koma dan 'dan' sebelum keluarga v-double-prime","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S226"}
